title: rotate croaks on a sops-written JSON number between int64max and uint64max
updated: 2026-08-21T03:24:42Z
---

Found while measuring karr #63 (sops 3.13.3 at /tmp/sops). NOT the same defect as #63 and deliberately kept out of its ADR 0020, because fixing it means reopening the int64 guard.

sops -e NORMALISES a JSON number wider than int64 by writing the float64 back out. For 9223372036854775808 it writes 9223372036854776000 -- which is still above int64max but BELOW uint64max, so Cpanel::JSON::XS decodes it as a Perl UV, detect_type calls it int, and Encrypted::assert_representable refuses it.

Measured, end to end:

  echo {"keep":"x","b_unencrypted":9223372036854775808} | sops -e   -> writes b_unencrypted: 9223372036854776000, exit 0
  sops -d of that file                                              -> exit 0
  File::SOPS->rotate of that file                                   -> CROAK, exit 255
      "value is an integer outside the range the SOPS int type can hold
       (-9223372036854775808 .. 9223372036854775807, Go)"

So this library refuses a document the reference implementation writes and reads. Same for encrypt of the plaintext, and the whole window [9223372036854775808 .. 18446744073709551615] behaves this way in JSON.

The guard is not simply wrong. Its stated reason holds for an ENCRYPTED slot: type:int with such a plaintext makes sops fail with strconv.Atoi out of range. It over-refuses for an UNENCRYPTED slot, where Go never calls Atoi -- it parses the JSON number into a float64 and digests FormatFloat of it. For 9223372036854776000 that text is the SAME as the digits, so the document would verify. For an arbitrary value in the window it is not, and the guard is right.

That is the shape of the fix and why it is not a one-liner: the answer depends on the slot, exactly as ADR 0008 and ADR 0012 argued for their guards, so it belongs at emit time and not in assert_representable. ADR 0020 changes nothing here.

YAML is different and already handled: go-yaml resolves this window as uint64, sops cannot walk it at all ("Cannot walk value, unknown type: uint64", exit 23) in either slot, and Format::YAML::_go_int already models that and refuses (ADR 0013). So sops cannot write a YAML document in this window -- only a JSON one.

Wire lane. Needs the sops binary to prove.
